h3:set-the-working-directory Set the working directory
fig:setwd Set the working directory in RStudio using the Session menu, so \\textbf{R} can locate your  \\emph{chapter2.r} script and \\emph{gdpfert.csv} dataset.
fig:fileschapter2 The Files pane in RStudio showing \\emph{chapter2.r} and \\emph{gdpfert.csv} after setting the working directory.
h3:writing-and-running-code-in-a-script-file Writing and running code in a script file
fig:scriptconsole The \\emph{chapter2.r} script file after it has been opened in RStudio.
h3:running-r-code-to-import-the-gdpfert.csv-dataset Running R code to import the gdpfert.csv dataset
h3:dataframes Dataframes
h3:rstudio-features-for-examining-datasets RStudio features for examining datasets
fig:environmentpane After importing \\emph{gdpfert.csv} the Environment pane displays the dataset with 214 observations and 13 variables, confirming a successful import.
h3:a-simple-scatterplot A simple scatterplot
fig:firstqplot Output of \\texttt{qplot()} showing GDP per capita and fertility rate for countries in the gdpfert.csv dataset.
h3:saving-data-in-an-r-workspace Saving data in an R Workspace
h2:authoring-a-data-analysis-report-rmarkdown Authoring a data analysis report: RMarkdown
fig:Rmarkdowncreate File menu in RStudio to select R Markdown and begin creating a new report.
fig:Rmarkdownname Dialog box for creating a new RMarkdown document. Enter a title and your name as the author.
fig:RMarkdownbase Default RMarkdown template, including a header, setup code chunk, narrative text, and an example \\textbf{R} code chunk.
fig:Rknitr Click the triangle next to the Knit button in RStudio to open the output format menu. Select Knit to Word to generate a Word document, which will appear in your working directory.
fig:codechunkmarkdown RMarkdown file prepared for use with \\textbf{R} code from the \\emph{chapter2.r} script. Replace the placeholder text inside the \\textbf{R} code chunk with your own analysis code. Any content within a code chunk (delimited by triple backticks) is treated as \\textbf{R} code.
